    "title": "How to Get Featured in Women's Journal | DNA PR",
    "description": "Women's Journal features women founders, executives and leaders. What it is, what a feature includes, and how to get featured.",
    "body": "<p>If you are a woman building a business, a practice or a personal brand, Women's Journal is one of the most aligned places your story can live.</p>\n<p>Here is what it is and how people get featured.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-women-s-journal-is\">What Women's Journal is</h2>\n<p>Women's Journal is a digital publication covering business, wellness, lifestyle and leadership, with a clear focus on women founders, executives and experts. Online only, permanently live, and indexed by search engines.</p>\n<p>Its readers come for perspective from women who are actually doing the work — which is exactly the position a feature puts you in.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-an-aligned-audience-matters-more-than-a-big-one\">Why an aligned audience matters more than a big one</h2>\n<p>A feature only pays off if it reaches people who can act on it.</p>\n<p>Women's Journal readers are already looking for the kind of expertise you sell. They are founders, professionals and decision-makers researching people worth following, hiring or buying from. That is a far shorter distance to a client than a general-interest audience ten times the size.</p>\n<p>Relevance converts. Reach alone does not.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-a-women-s-journal-feature-includes\">What a Women's Journal feature includes</h2>\n<p>A solo, dedicated article about you and your work, with a headline and angle built around your positioning. Typically photos and links to your website, LinkedIn and socials.</p>\n<p>It publishes permanently and stays indexed, so it keeps working every time someone searches your name.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-to-get-featured\">How to get featured</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Pitch directly.</strong> Free and legitimate, dependent on fit and editorial capacity.</li><li><strong>Use a professional feature service.</strong> A team writes it to the publication's standard and places it. Faster and more predictable, which is why most founders choose it.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"what-makes-a-strong-women-s-journal-piece\">What makes a strong Women's Journal piece</h2>\n<p>The features that land here are generous with insight.</p>\n<p>Readers want to know what you have actually learned — building the business, serving the client, making the difficult call. Specifics beat adjectives every time. One real story about a decision you got wrong and what changed afterward is worth more than a page of credentials.</p>\n<p>Write for the reader who is a few steps behind you, and the authority takes care of itself.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-to-expect-from-the-process\">What to expect from the process</h2>\n<p>Share your story, our team drafts the piece, you review with revisions until it is exactly right, and nothing publishes until you approve it. Then it goes live and you get the link to share.</p>\n<p>Any provider who cannot show you the draft first is not one to use.</p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-started\">Getting started</h2>\n<p>Digital Networking Agency works with Women's Journal and a wide network of publications. We write, edit and place. You keep full editorial control, and nothing goes live without your sign-off.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Who is Women's Journal for?</h3>\n<p>Women founders, executives, coaches, consultants and experts building authority — and the readers researching people like them.</p>\n<h3>What makes a strong Women's Journal feature?</h3>\n<p>Real, specific insight from your own experience rather than a list of achievements. Write for the reader a few steps behind you.</p>\n<h3>Can I approve the article before it publishes?</h3>\n<p>Yes. You review and revise until it is right, and nothing publishes without your approval.</p>",
