    "slug": "how-to-get-featured-in-fox-interviewer",
    "h1": "How to Get Featured in Fox Interviewer",
    "title": "How to Get Featured in Fox Interviewer | DNA PR",
    "description": "Fox Interviewer is an independent digital publication, not Fox News. What it is, what a feature includes, and how to get featured.",
    "body": "<p>If you want a feature where you actually get to speak, rather than be summarised, Fox Interviewer is worth understanding.</p>\n<p>Here is what it is and how to get featured.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-fox-interviewer-is\">What Fox Interviewer is</h2>\n<p>Fox Interviewer is a digital news publication launched in 2018 and based in Detroit, Michigan. It covers business, technology, politics, healthcare, lifestyle and trending news, with a strong emphasis on interviews and profiles of founders, executives and subject-matter experts. Online only, permanently live, and indexed by search engines.</p>\n<p><strong>An important clarification.</strong> Fox Interviewer is independent. It is not affiliated with, owned by, or endorsed by Fox News, Fox Corporation or Fox Broadcasting. The names are similar and searchers confuse them constantly, so it is worth being direct: a Fox Interviewer feature is a Fox Interviewer feature, and describing it as Fox News coverage is a misrepresentation that will cost you more credibility than the feature ever earns you.</p>\n<p>Understood for what it is, it is a legitimate digital outlet with a real readership across business and technology.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-an-interview-format-works\">Why an interview format works</h2>\n<p>Most coverage flattens you. Your story gets compressed, and what survives is a line of paraphrase.</p>\n<p>An interview format does the opposite. Q&amp;A and interview-led features give your personality and expertise room to come through in your own words — your reasoning, your phrasing, the way you actually explain what you do.</p>\n<p>That matters because people trust voice. A reader can tell the difference between someone describing an expert and an expert speaking. When a prospect or a partner reads the piece, they meet you rather than a summary of you.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-a-feature-includes\">What a feature includes</h2>\n<p>A dedicated interview or profile article built around you and your work, with a headline and angle shaped by your positioning. Typically a photo or two and several links to your website, LinkedIn and socials.</p>\n<p>It publishes permanently and stays indexed, becoming a reference point every time someone researches you before a meeting or a decision.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-to-get-featured\">How to get featured</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Pitch directly.</strong> Free and legitimate, dependent on fit and editorial capacity.</li><li><strong>Use a professional feature service.</strong> A team develops the angle, writes it to the publication's standard and places it. Faster and more predictable, which is why most founders choose it — their constraint is time.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"what-makes-a-strong-piece\">What makes a strong piece</h2>\n<p>The best interview features sound like someone talking, not someone marketing.</p>\n<p>Give real answers. Explain how you think about a problem, what you got wrong before you got it right, what you believe about your market that most people in it do not. Specifics beat adjectives. \"We grew fast\" is nothing; the decision behind the growth is a story.</p>\n<p>If a reader finishes the piece feeling like they have met you and learned something, it has worked. That is the whole brief.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-to-expect-from-the-process\">What to expect from the process</h2>\n<p>Share your story and perspective, our team drafts the piece, you review with revisions until it is exactly right, and nothing publishes until you approve it. Then it goes live and you get the link to share.</p>\n<p>Any provider who cannot show you the draft first is not one to use.</p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-started\">Getting started</h2>\n<p>Digital Networking Agency works with Fox Interviewer and a wide network of digital publications. We develop the angle, write, edit and place. You keep full editorial control, and nothing goes live without your sign-off.</p>\n<p>If you want a feature where your own voice does the work, this is a good place for it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Is Fox Interviewer affiliated with Fox News?</h3>\n<p>No. Fox Interviewer is an independent digital publication with no affiliation to, ownership by, or endorsement from Fox News, Fox Corporation or Fox Broadcasting. A feature there should never be described as Fox News coverage.</p>\n<h3>What does Fox Interviewer cover?</h3>\n<p>Business, technology, politics, healthcare, lifestyle and trending news, with a particular focus on interviews and profiles of founders and experts.</p>\n<h3>Can I approve the article before it publishes?</h3>\n<p>Yes. You review and revise until it is right, and nothing publishes without your approval.</p>",
